preserved.`","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate `inbound_differ.py` and `applier.py` (re-import + `__all__` re-export of `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL`) as consumers to update when the inbound literal is retired for the shared parse helper.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0556,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach §4 lists inbound sites as inbound_fields, inbound_translate, apply_inbound_events ('the four sites can't drift') and speaks of retiring the 'duplicated literal'.","inbound_differ.py:54 `from rebar_reconciler.inbound_fields import (... _REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL ...)` (noqa F401 re-import).","applier.py:150 imports `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` from inbound_translate and applier.py:307 lists it in `__all__`.","Neither inbound_differ.py nor applier.py appears in the Scope (files) list."],"finding":"The plan retires the `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literal in inbound_fields/inbound_translate in favor of a shared parse helper, but two consumers that import that symbol by name are not enumerated: inbound_differ.py re-imports it and applier.py re-imports AND re-exports it in `__all__`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f30061c8fb6adcc2a","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach §4 / Scope (files)","norm_id":"n8f130ca5685f3ce5","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the literal dict is deleted from inbound_fields.py / inbound_translate.py, inbound_differ.py and applier.py fail at import time (ImportError) on the now-missing name, and the config parity/attribute-access tests that rely on the applier re-export break."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either keep `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` as a derived/compat name so the re-exports stay valid, or add inbound_differ.py and applier.py to Scope with the import/`__all__` fixups.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the collapse-set stamping rule selects the single un-annotated canonical member of each collapse group (so the built-in map still stamps ONLY blocked/cancelled and does not gain rebar-status:in_progress/closed/deleted), and state this preservation in the collapse round-trip test oracle.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the collapse set = local statuses sharing a Jira target with another local status; stamp rebar-status:<local> for any status in it (default blocked/cancelled is a special case, so default behaviour is preserved)'","value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA: in_progress->'In Progress', blocked->'In Progress'; closed->'Done', cancelled->'Done', deleted->'Done' — so the built-in collapse set includes in_progress/closed/deleted, not just blocked/cancelled","config.py:52-60 documents the invariant: 'The canonical preimage is the UNANNOTATED local status — blocked/cancelled are reconstructed from rebar-status: annotation labels'","Today's _STATUS_ANNOTATION_LABEL (outbound_labels.py:88) stamps ONLY blocked/cancelled"],"finding":"The generalised collapse-set rule ('stamp rebar-status:<local> for any status in the collapse set') is under-specified for how it preserves default behaviour: on the built-in map the collapse set is {in_progress, blocked, closed, cancelled, deleted} (in_progress/blocked share 'In Progress'; closed/cancelled/deleted share 'Done'), so a naive reading would stamp rebar-status:in_progress/closed/deleted in addition to today's blocked/cancelled — a default-path behaviour change that contradicts the 'bit-for-bit preserved' claim. The plan calls default blocked/cancelled 'a special case' but does not state the mechanism that selects the single UNANNOTATED (canonical-preimage) member of each collapse group which must NOT be stamped.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe2bcac38edfaaea8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 (Generalised rebar-status: collapse round-trip) / outbound_labels.py","norm_id":"nd38b426bbae6df76","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A default (no [mapping] config) reconcile pass on a ticket whose local status is in_progress or closed","The Rollback/expand-contract claim that with no [mapping] section behaviour is 'bit-for-bit preserved'"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Define the stamp set as: for each Jira target with multiple local preimages, designate exactly one canonical (un-annotated) preimage — matching config.py's 'canonical preimage' via the effective reverse map's value for that target — and stamp rebar-status:<local> only for the NON-canonical members. On the built-in map this yields exactly {blocked, cancelled}.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` reference inventory via `find_referencing_symbols` (plus a name grep) and add inbound_differ.py:54 and applier.py:150/:307 to Scope, deciding whether each re-export/`__all__` entry is 